  "text": "Classic Neapolitan ice cream is a traditional Italian dessert made with three distinct flavors: **Vanilla**, **Chocolate**, and **Stracciatella** (a soft, creamy custard-based ice cream with chocolate shavings). It\u2019s often served in a single serving, swirls of the three flavors mixed together by hand, symbolizing a tricolor flag (like Italy's national flag). Here's a simple and authentic recipe to make Neapolitan ice cream at home:\n\n---\n\n### \ud83c\udf66 **Classic Neapolitan Ice Cream (Simple Recipe)**\n\n#### **Ingredients** (for 2\u20133 servings):\n- 2 cups (400g) heavy cream\n- 1 cup (250ml) whole milk\n- 3/4 cup (60g) granulated sugar\n- 1/2 cup (120ml) vanilla extract or 2 vanilla beans (split and scraped)\n- 1/2 cup (60g) cocoa powder (for chocolate flavor)\n- 2 egg yolks (for chocolate flavor)\n- 1/2 cup (120ml) hot water (for chocolate flavor)\n- 1/4 tsp salt\n- 1/2 tsp vanilla extract (for vanilla)\n\n---\n\n### \ud83e\uddfd **Steps:**\n\n#### **1. Make Vanilla Ice Cream:**\n- In a medium saucepan, combine:\n  - 1/2 cup (120ml) heavy cream\n  - 1/2 cup (120ml) whole milk\n  - 1/2 cup (60g) sugar\n  - 1/2 tsp vanilla extract\n  - 1/4 tsp salt\n\n- Whisk until the sugar dissolves. Heat over medium heat until it starts to simmer, then remove from heat.\n\n- In a clean bowl, whisk egg yolks and set aside.\n\n- Slowly pour the hot cream mixture into the egg yolks, stirring continuously to temper the eggs.\n\n- Return to the saucepan and cook over medium heat, stirring constantly, until the mixture thickens and reaches 170\u00b0F (77\u00b0C) or until it coats the back of a spoon.\n\n- Cool the mixture completely in the refrigerator for at least 4 hours, or until chilled.\n\n- Churn in an ice cream maker according to the manufacturer\u2019s instructions until it reaches a soft-serve consistency.\n\n---\n\n#### **2. Make Chocolate Ice Cream:**\n- In a medium saucepan, combine:\n  - 1/2 cup (120ml) heavy cream\n  - 1/2 cup (120ml) whole milk\n  - 1/2 cup (60g) sugar\n  - 1/2 cup (60g) cocoa powder\n  - 1/4 tsp salt\n  - 2 egg yolks\n  - 1/2 cup (120ml) hot water\n\n- Whisk the egg yolks and sugar until well combined.\n\n- Add the cocoa powder and hot water, then gradually pour in the hot cream and milk mixture, whisking constantly.\n\n- Cook over low heat, stirring constantly, until the mixture thickens and reaches 170\u00b0F (77\u00b0C) or until it coats the back of a spoon.\n\n- Cool the mixture in the refrigerator for at least 4 hours, or until chilled.\n\n- Churn in an ice cream maker until it reaches a soft-serve consistency.\n\n---\n\n#### **3. Make Stracciatella Ice Cream (Optional):**\n- In a clean bowl, whisk:\n  - 1 cup (240ml) heavy cream\n  - 1/2 cup (120ml) whole",
